00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:32.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:32.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:32.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.730
Episode 3
A Loner? Are You Kidding Me?!

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.790
I feel ostracized already.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:53.750
That's this year's only scholarship 
student of magic, Baumeister.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.710
Magic users are rare enough as is,

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:02.260
but I've heard his magic power is already 
on par with top-class adventurers.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:07.820
I heard that the magic instructor decided
 there was nothing more he could teach him,

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.220
and gave up on instructing him.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:14.190
If you party up with that guy,
 you're set for life.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.940
You know how it goes, right?

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.770
Most of the parties from the 
Academy continue to stay together

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:22.480
even after they graduate 
and become adventurers.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.580
Looks like everyone's thinking the same thing.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.120
Party Registration Form
Name                                               Specialty
Erwin von Arnim                           Sword

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.120
So I have a proposal for you two.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.410
Hey! You wrote my name on it!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.270
Listen, that guy's currently appraising us.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:42.590
He's trying to decide if we're 
worthy of a great mage like him.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.880
Oh! So that's why he's always alone!

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.560
Huh? You really think so?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.980
That's why we do this.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:57.020
If you two, the top martial artist and 
spearwoman, join me, the top swordsman,

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.680
don't you think even he might recognize us?

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:03.650
Hey!

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.450
It's not a bad idea.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.160
Huh? You're kidding. 
You plan to form a party with him?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.220
I'm the fifth son of the 
Arnim Knightdom, Erwin von Arnim.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.390
You can call me "Er."

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.880
I'm Louise. This is Iina, my friend 
since childhood. Nice to meet you!

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.570
Huh?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.110
Muster up your courage...

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.980
Blend into the class more!

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.860
U-Um, hey...

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:36.260
This is called sansho pepper.
If you'd like some...

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.810
I see. So you guys are after the same thing.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:48.200
Too bad, though, because he's going 
to recognize us, the axe trio!

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.260
They're laughing and having so much fun...

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.930
I probably shouldn't bother right now.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:05.040
Now, I'm sure some of you here aren't 
receiving a stipend from your family

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.470
and have to work part-time 
to earn your living.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:10.430
That's me.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:14.690
Our academy recommends 
hunting in such cases,

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:19.900
but since it's dangerous to hunt alone, 
make sure you go in groups if you do.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.710
In groups?

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.670
There's no room for me anywhere.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.170
Hey, what do you think?

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.950
Should we say something to Baumeister?

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:34.290
No, let's be careful about this.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:40.620
If we're too hasty and make a mistake that 
disappoints him, it will all be for naught.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:46.050
Though... I notice he's not speaking to anyone.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.510
That's it! This is a 
challenge from Baumeister!

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.470
Huh?! What do you mean?!

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.580
This is what he's trying to say:

00:06:55.580 --> 00:07:01.520
"You should have no trouble bringing in more 
prey as a group than I could hunting alone."

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.440
So if a group brings back less prey than him...

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:10.520
Then that group will removed 
from his list of candidates.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:19.840
Here you go.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.840
We should be okay with this much.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:33.510
Still, you two really are the 
daughters of great masters.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:36.950
Have you both been training with 
your families since you were little?

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:38.850
Yeah.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:43.560
B-But you were awesome with your sword, too!

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.320
Well, I come from a poor knightdom,

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:52.030
so I've been training with the sword 
like crazy ever since I was a kid.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.300
Oh, excuse me. Coming through.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:58.950
Huh? Where's his prey?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.660
Oh, a magic bag, huh?

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.900
Where did you get one of those?

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.960
Oh, my master left it to me.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:07.750
Hup!

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.310
Wh-Whoa... Wait a...

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.750
Hmph. This is dumb.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.120
I'm out.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:22.760
Huh?

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.890
He lives in a whole different world.

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.880
With this much difference 
between our skill levels,

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.100
it'll be impossible to earn his recognition.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.240
It's not worth the effort.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.280
You all get it too, right?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.240
If you're not the eldest son,

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.200
it's wiser to not bother dreaming of more.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.300
This is a big help! 
They're all precious bounties.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.510
I hope you'll come again.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:51.270
Sure!

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.660
If you're interested, let's grab a bite 
to eat together with this mo—

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.410
...ney?

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.690
My brother once said something similar.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.620
He said that no matter how hard 
I trained with the sword,

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:12.580
a fifth son will never inherit.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:15.270
That I was just wasting my effort.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.450
It was the same for Louise and me.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.860
No matter how strong we were,

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.580
we couldn't inherit the school 
because we weren't eldest sons.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.090
It's the same everywhere, huh?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.490
It would be one thing if that were all it was.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:34.960
The truth is, both of us were born with 
a bit more magic power than most people.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:39.340
I mean, not that it's enough 
just that we can <i>use</i> magic,

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.660
but if we use that magic to 
enhance our physical abilities...

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.520
Then a normal person stands no chance, huh?

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:52.740
Before I knew it, I was stronger 
than my father and brother,

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.450
and at some point, they began avoiding me.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.440
So I ended up having to train in secret.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.400
I can't accept this!

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:08.800
Why on earth does being born later 
mean we're not allowed to dream?!

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:09.960
That's just wrong, isn't it?!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.180
I'm not giving up.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:19.480
At this point, let's hunt lots of big game 
and make sure Baumeister recognizes us!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.770
If you're after big game, 
this is the place! Deep in the forest!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:31.250
The teacher told us we weren't allowed 
to go in here, but we have no choice!

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.220
We do have a choice.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:34.980
Come on, let's turn back.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:38.660
They're here.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:39.840
Wolves.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.160
Extra-large ones, at that.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:06.950
Wolves, and... those are... people?

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:13.380
If those are my classmates, maybe 
we can become friends if I save them!

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:29.750
Damn it! How many of them are there?!

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.590
I'm sorry. We should have listened to Iina.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:35.130
Louise, above you!

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:41.550
Er!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.620
What in the world...

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.200
Are you okay?

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:07.910
We're sorry.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.930
It's fine. I mean, we're classmates, after all.

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.950
We were trying to get you to recognize us,

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.550
but we just made trouble for you.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:17.900
Huh?

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:19.050
Me?

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.400
After seeing that magic you used, though,

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:26.890
I realized we really do 
live in different worlds.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:28.820
So...

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:29.980
H-Hey...

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.980
I'm giving up on forming a party with you now.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:35.460
With me?!

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.530
We haven't given up on everything, though.

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:42.950
We'll find some other way 
to pave a brighter future.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.410
Uh, h-h-hang on a second...

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:47.180
So this is where you—

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:49.680
What happened?

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.060
Oh, it's just a scratch.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.500
Anyway, did you need us for something?

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.810
Oh...

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:59.090
Rejoice! All the students 
of our scholarship class

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:03.800
have been invited to a garden party 
hosted by the Duke of Bleichröder!

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:08.260
A chance to meet the Duke 
of Bleichröder in person!

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:13.090
He's one of the nobles currently competing 
for the top in the Kingdom of Helmut.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:16.800
If he takes a liking to us, it could 
open up the path to becoming a retainer!

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.440
What are you all excited about?

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:23.520
We're obviously only being invited
 because the Duke of Bleichröder

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:29.740
wants to lay claim to our 
great mage, Baumeister.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.200
We're just extras.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.980
Then there's no way he's going 
to take an interest in us.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.670
What? Then there's no point 
in getting excited over this.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.130
Huh?

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.310
Really?

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:42.840
That's all?

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.070
That's disappointing.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:50.720
All right! Let's go buy outfits 
for the garden party together!

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.140
Formal wear, huh?

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:55.890
That'll cost us a lot, but it is for our future.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.610
Oh, come on. Are you all still 
getting your hopes up?

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.820
What's wrong with that?

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:07.030
There's still some chance, right?

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.990
Hey, maybe he'll speak to 
us if we go in showy outfits!

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.750
You can do that, Louise.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:15.440
I'm going in something normal.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:16.590
Why?!

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.910
Let's all go in something showy!

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:20.980
Sorry, I can't do that.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.110
What?!

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.380
Party Registration Form

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.380
Name

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.380
Specialty

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.380
Member Name

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.380
Specialty

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:37.920
Oh, there he is!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:38.940
Look, over there!

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:42.060
Duke Bleichröder...

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:46.030
That's Duke Bleichröder?

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:00.080
He's coming! He's coming! He's coming!

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.580
He's coming this way, Iina!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:02.330
Yeah.

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.550
U-Um, I...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.640
A pleasure to meet you.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:18.000
I am Amadeus Freytag von Bleichröder.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.630
I'm Wendelin von Benno Baumeister.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.620
My, it's good to see someone 
from the Baumeisters,

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:30.140
our vassals, visiting us here in Breichburg.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:36.600
The Baumeisters so rarely 
participate in gatherings like this.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:41.540
Well, as you know, our family's 
financial affairs are strained.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:45.340
There is some expense involved
in crossing those mountains.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.070
But some of my other vassals complain that

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:52.150
it's rude for them to refuse 
their lord's invitation.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.970
My apologies.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.920
Well, enough about that.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.430
The truth is, I was hoping to speak with you.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.900
Could I have a bit of your time?

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:06.860
Very well.

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:08.300
Then let's go over here.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.020
Excuse me!

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.620
Um, there are some people 
I'd like to bring with me.

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:16.900
These three.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.660
They're my party members.

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:40.220
This is my court magician.

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:45.630
Brantag Ringstat.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:47.670
Nice to meet you.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:54.110
He was also the teacher to my former 
court magician, Alfred Rainford.

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:58.240
Well, truth be told,

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:04.580
Alfred died in the Enchanted Forest near
 your family's lands an awfully long time ago.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.040
It seems he later became a Whispering Dead.

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:10.770
But I was still his master.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:13.920
I always kept an eye on the 
presence of my disciple.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.340
Brantag is a talented user of tracking magic.

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:22.680
He's able to track the magic power of anyone 
he's met in person over great distances.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:24.810
It was seven years ago.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.150
That was when Alfred's presence 
suddenly disappeared.

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.290
He was a Whispering Dead,

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:34.110
so I thought perhaps he had 
fulfilled his wish and passed on,

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:37.080
but then I remembered that 
while he was alive he told me,

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:41.220
"I want to meet someone to whom I can 
pass on all the magic I've learned."

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.770
So I thought it over and 
realized that if that was

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:48.120
the wish he had clung to, 
then it was never coming true.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:52.200
He had a greater magic capacity 
than even me, his master,

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:56.590
and he was counted amongst the top 
five magicians on this continent.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:18:01.950
There was no way he would ever find a 
magician he could recognize as his disciple.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:08.030
Yet now, here is a man with 
incredible magic power

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:11.310
from the very same region where 
his presence disappeared.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.460
A man carrying his magic bag, no less.

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.790
Pardon me, but what are 
the chances he stole it?

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:22.430
Not possible.

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:29.290
No one could use that magic bag unless 
Alfred himself had transferred ownership.

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:31.820
You're it, aren't you?

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:34.670
You're Alfred's disciple.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:36.660
Yes.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.010
Then there's one thing I'd like to ask you.

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.600
What were his final moments like?

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:59.740
I purged my master before 
he could become a zombie.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:03.980
Damn. What a thing to force upon a child...

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:09.700
Thank you.

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:11.290
Because of you,

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:15.120
he was able to pass on peacefully.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:19.930
No, I...

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:25.250
Oh, right.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.850
This bag that my master carried
 contains the supplies

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:32.470
meant for the 2,000-man expedition
 to the Enchanted Forest.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:37.210
I've been meaning to return 
it for a while now.

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:42.160
We didn't know anything about him.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:47.640
He did mention that he had lived by himself 
to avoid a struggle over succession.

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:51.400
That's the same as us...

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.730
Yet we said that he lived in another world.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:58.630
Hey!

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.190
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:06.150
It took more time than I thought 
to hand over those supplies.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:10.630
Hey, what you said about us being a party...

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:15.320
Yeah, sorry to spring that on you. I just—

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:18.480
We don't deserve to be in a party with you!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.530
We were all planning to use you.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:27.660
To make you a tool to 
improve our own lives.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.620
Oh, but that kind of goes both ways.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:32.460
Huh?

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:37.520
I dragged you all along without warning 
because I didn't want to go anywhere

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:39.540
alone with an old guy of his standing.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.050
Huh?!

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:44.510
Then when you said we were a party...

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:46.620
Oh, no, no!

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.970
I really did want to be in 
a party with you three!

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.920
But why us?

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:59.430
Well, because it seems like 
I'd have fun with you three,

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:01.150
even when things get tough.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.180
Huh?

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:06.930
Well, long ago, my master told me that I have

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.870
what it takes to enjoy what 
the wide world has to offer.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:14.630
So I thought it would be good to have 
friends who could enjoy it with me.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:18.040
Huh? That's your reason?

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:21.500
Sorry. That's my reason.

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.960
I can't believe that's what 
you'd recognize us for.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:34.180
We nearly got ourselves eaten by wolves!

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:37.520
Jeez! This is all your fault, Well!

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.140
Hey, you just called me "Well"...

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:45.580
I'm sorry, I forgot something very important.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:46.150
Yes?

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:51.970
The reward for returning those supplies 
meant for 2,000 men is 20% of their value,

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:55.140
so I'll be sending you 1,000 gold coins later.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:57.060
1,000 gold coins?!

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:01.230
Uh, one gold coin is worth 
roughly one million yen,

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:04.650
so a thousand is... a billion yen or so...

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:07.110
What?!

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:10.520
Also, Alfred had his own estate.

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:13.560
We've made arrangements for you to inherit it.

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:16.740
Master's... estate?

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:29.400
This is too big for a 
student living on his own.

00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:35.220
I wonder if anyone will share it with me...

